<title>SWEDEN: Stadshypotek posts flat '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Stadshypotek posts flat '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's largest mortgage bank Stadshypotek AB reports for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  3,016 vs   3,067</p>
<p> Net interest income		     4,311 vs   4,799</p>
<p> Credit losses				 575 vs   1,072</p>
<p>(includes property value changes)  </p>
<p> Total income				4,722 vs   5,171</p>
<p> Operating costs/overhead		1,131 vs   1,032</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     3,591 vs   4,139</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,154 vs   2,194</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				17.66 vs   17.98</p>
<p>NOTE - Stadshypotek is currently under a 22.9 billion cash takeover bid by Swedish commercial bank Handelsbanken that is due to close on February 14. Handelsbanken has offered 180 crowns per B-series share and 190 crowns per A-series share. Stadshypotek board has recommended shareholders accept the offer.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
